      "id": "text-3",
      "type": "text",
      "content": {
        "heading": "Oily Sponsors",
        "body": "Eni’s annual fossil fuel emissions could melt enough glacier ice to fill 2.5 million Olympic swimming pools. Meanwhile, more than half of the potential host cities for Winter Games will become \"climate-unreliable\" by the 2080s due to the climate crisis.\n\n‍\n\nIt's clear: One cannot sponsor the winter games while at the same time fuel its collapse. This isn’t sponsorship, it’s sportswashing."
      },
      "padTop": "4-5"
    },
    {
      "id": "cta-4",
      "type": "cta",
      "content": {
        "image": {
          "src": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6465c08bc2eb8d26649eade8/698150aea25a5ea1425ce47c_Oilympics_2.10.2-optimized.jpg",
          "alt": ""
        },
        "heading": "Get Involved",
        "text": "Add your name to Greenpeace's petition and demand the International Olympic Committee drop all oil and gas sponsorship.",
        "button": {
          "label": "Act to Demand Polluters Pay",
          "href": "https://www.greenpeace.org/international/act/winter-olympics/?_gl=1*12vd3rh*_up*MQ..*_ga*OTc0MTQ1NTY1LjE3NzAxMTE1NTM.*_ga_94MRTN8HG4*czE3NzAxMTE1NTMkbzEkZzAkdDE3NzAxMTE1NTMkajYwJGwwJGgyMzUzNzY5ODM."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "quote-5",
      "type": "quote",
      "content": {
        "quote": "\"We wish for the Winter Olympics what we wish for our planet: cold winters, real snow and ice, keeping our Planet cool and the Winter Games alive. Fossil fuel companies like Eni, an official sponsor of the 2026 Winter Olympics, are actively ruining that future for all of us.\"",
        "cite": "Directors Jorik Dozy & Sil van der Woerd"
      },
      "padBottom": "4-5"
    },
